    },
    {
      "id": "ac79bcc05ee6b67ae4467112e59b2895eb360458",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3311674307,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This is only for Windows and macOS, so it doesn't affect Unix. Yes, the glib-bundle for Windows includes libxml2 too, I assume because both libxml2 (for now) and glib depend on zlib.\n\nThere's still some extra dependencies that way, the vcpkg package for minizip-ng depends on zlib (not zlib-ng) and on zstd, so it is a bit odd to have separate packages for those for Windows. It \"works\" so long as they depend on the same DLLs, even though we end up downloading the same DLLs multiple times.\n\nThere's something really complicated with libssh (which we use only for some extcap binaries) - the libssh vcpkg builds against OpenSSL, and to avoid introducing some license issues we prefer to build against libgcrypt, which means building our own package or alternating the libssh recipe from vcpkg. We build our own using MSYS2, but since libssh also depends on zlib, this can create some issues because zlib 1.3.2 renamed the DLL on Windows by default for various reasons.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-05-04T14:11:25.885Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-05-04T14:11:25.885Z",
